<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-1159] Redundant MVCC queue iteration may be removed</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-1159</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;When MVCC lock candidates are added for multiple keys, they are linked together to ensure proper lock acquisition order. The linkage is done in GridCacheMvccManager#addNext()&lt;br/&gt;
The manager contains a thread-local queue of previously added candidates which is reset after each message. When a candidate is added, addNext() iterates over the queue and unlinks used candidates.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The drawback of this code is that on large batches of size N (say, a batch of 100 values) the code will execute N^2 operations which dramatically reduces performance of bulk transactions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It looks like that this code is unnecessary because:&lt;br/&gt;
1) Candidates cannot become used while lock request being processed.&lt;br/&gt;
2) There is no need to unlink as the candidates will be GCed after locks are released.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
